## 4. Investment Thesis & Peer Comparison
CVS is a core player in healthcare with strong market share in PBM and retail pharmacies. However, its ability to sustain margins amid regulatory and competitive pressures is uncertain. Compared to UnitedHealth Group (UNH), CVS trades at a lower P/FCF multiple but has weaker growth prospects.  

**Bull Case:** Regulatory headwinds ease, and CVS leverages its scale to regain pricing power in generics and PBM services.  
**Bear Case:** Margins continue to erode as Amazon gains market share, and regulatory fines weigh on profitability.  

**Verdict:** WATCH — attractive valuation but uncertain execution.

